[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:70. Red for Danger]
[00:00.340]Passage 70 | 文章七十
[00:01.790]Red for danger. | 危险的红色
[00:04.540]During a bullfight, a drunk suddenly wandered into the middle of the ring. | 在斗牛时，一个醉汉突然晃晃悠悠地走到斗牛场中央。
[00:11.105]The crowd began to shout, | 人群开始叫喊，
[00:13.550]but the drunk was unaware of the danger. | 但醉汉却没有意识到危险。
[00:16.725]The bull was busy with the matador at the time, | 这时公牛正忙于对付斗牛士，
[00:20.515]but it'd suddenly caught sight of the drunk, | 却突然看到了那个醉汉，
[00:23.625]who was shouting rude remarks | 他正在大声喊叫着粗鲁的话语，
[00:25.950]and waving a red cap. | 挥舞着一顶红帽子。
[00:28.375]Apparently sensitive to criticism, | 显然是对批评很敏感，
[00:31.700]the bull forgot all about the matador | 公牛完全忘记了斗牛士，
[00:34.405]and charged at the drunk. | 向醉汉冲去。
[00:36.885]The crowd suddenly grew quiet. | 人群突然安静下来。
[00:40.245]The drunk, however, | 然而，那个醉汉
[00:42.220]seemed quite sure of himself. | 似乎对自己很有把握。
[00:44.690]When the bull got close to him, | 当公牛靠近他时，
[00:47.205]he clumsily stepped aside to let it pass. | 他笨拙地退到一边，让公牛过去。
[00:50.725]The crowd broke into cheers, | 人群爆发出欢呼声，
[00:53.555]and the drunk bowed. | 醉汉鞠了一躬。
[00:55.475]By this time, however, | 然而，这时，
[00:57.600]three men had come into the ring, | 三个人已经进入了斗牛场，
[00:59.930]and they quickly dragged the drunk to safety. | 他们迅速将醉汉拖到安全地带。
[01:03.295]Even the bull seemed to feel sorry for him, | 甚至公牛似乎也为他感到遗憾，
[01:06.715]for it looked on sympathetically | 因为它同情地看着，
[01:09.160]until the drunk was out of the way, | 直到醉汉离开，
[01:11.410]before once more turning its attention to the matador. | 才再次将注意力转向斗牛士。